TYPES.md §12.1, §3.6: a method written in a variant body outside any case shares every case's names, so one named like a field of a case is E2104, at the variant-level method; a name no case uses is fine.
-- a/a.canon --
package a

local variant Reward {
  item { count: Int }
  gold { amount: Int }
  nothing

  fn count(self) -> Int { return 1 }

  fn worth(self) -> Int { return 2 }
}
-- findings.txt --
error[E2104]  a/a.canon:8:6
  Reward.item has a field and a method named count

1 error, 0 warnings in 1 package (…)
